{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter","id":982644,"title":"Updated Changeling Rules Chapter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-06T05:55:28-07:00","id":982644,"title":"Updated Changeling Rules Chapter","content":"I'm getting ready for final editing and stuff like layout.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyoY0lxSjZQZXhyNGc\" target=\"_blank\">This is Chapter 3</a>, which is basically almost all the player-facing mechanics. Creation, Merits, Pledges, Tokens, Dreams, Goblin Fruits, Contracts, the core template material. All that jazz. Consider this the companion piece to the Seemings and Kiths I posted last week.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyoY0lxSjZQZXhyNGc\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2...0lxSjZQZXhyNGc</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:04:45-07:00","id":982648,"title":"","content":"So mask and mien are back to virtue and vice again. I must say I prefer the mask / mien version, though the names did need a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:22:55-07:00","id":982653,"title":"","content":"I must say, I love that Changelings apparent age is proportional to their increased lifespan, and that it applies retroactively and can cause them to de-age. It gives weight to the mythical childlike appearance of fairies and elves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:25:52-07:00","id":982655,"title":"","content":"Mask and Mien are still in there in the Changeling Rules section, following Character Creation which refers to Virtue and Vice instead.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure whether Legendary Language is new to this version or I just missed the update with it since I haven't been following that closely. It's phrased like it's meant to be very broad but not infinite, but I have a hard time imagining any significant languages it wouldn't yield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T07:02:07-07:00","id":982671,"title":"","content":"Nice!<br /> Just.. one thing... the &quot;Defensive Dreamscaping&quot; merit. Is it supposed to work in real life as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T07:45:15-07:00","id":982686,"title":"","content":"I really like the entitlement rules, the scaling power of them based on the difficulty of joining is a great way of doing it.<br /> <br /> Tokens I like, but I think there either needs to be a lot more examples or more solid guidelines on how to make your own tokens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:00:43-07:00","id":982697,"title":"","content":"Thank you dave","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:30:19-07:00","id":982706,"title":"","content":"Thank you for sharing this! I'm a little confused about the Anchors though. Are we going with Virtue &amp; Vice like with mortals &amp; mages, or are we using the Mask &amp; Mein detailed after the creation summary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:17:30-07:00","id":982772,"title":"","content":"The Dream rules changes are innteresting. Changelings end up being rather resilient there! The Iron weakness is a bit simpler in application than I was expecting after the discussions of what is perceived as iron qualifying as such, though. Which may be for the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:41:45-07:00","id":982782,"title":"","content":"I think a Wittgensteinien definition of Iron is really the best way to go. If you try to define it based on chemical composition or quality or what have you, there's no meaningful way of separating iron from steel, because technically speaking steel is literally just Fe with very little C. But, if you go by the philosophical concept of Cluster Concepts and Family Resemblance, it's hard to argue that steel is a paradigm case of iron; otherwise we wouldn't call it steel, we would just call it iron, maybe with a qualifier like &quot;fine iron&quot;. Between the fringe case of steel and the paradigm case of cold iron, you get wrought iron, pig iron, iron ore, etc. those all fall somewhere in-between, and different groups can decide for themselves what exactly qualifies and what doesn't, including just saying steel counts if that's how your group wants to handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-06-2016, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:35:42-07:00","id":982856,"title":"","content":"One oddity I noticed, there's the 'Hedgespun' merit at 1+ with some flexible options for creating clothes, weapons, or other things, but there's also the 'Gossamer Raiment' 1-3 dot token that is roughly the same thing but without the creation options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:12:57-07:00","id":982876,"title":"","content":"Lot of great stuff so far. One rules-niggle I have!<br /> <br /> ELEMENTAL BATTLE requires possessing certain contracts and makes them more-powerful.. but do the techniques require you to activate those Contracts? For example, does Level 3 require Cloak to be up to throw elemental attacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11533-bluegrass-beast","name":"Bluegrass Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:50:56-07:00","id":982906,"title":"","content":"Also, I do not see Become the Primal Foundation listed; is it meant to be Phantom Glory, which absorbed elemental transformations in its Elemental affinity power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11533-bluegrass-beast","name":"Bluegrass Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:23:41-07:00","id":982928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=982648#post982648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So mask and mien are back to virtue and vice again. I must say I prefer the mask / mien version, though the names did need a change.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, I like Virtue/Vice better-because it implies that changelings are still, at their core, human enough. It emphasizes that<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/85/a2/ce/85a2ce1f069147e318d84bfb32ab5cfb.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> God I love Undertale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:02:23-07:00","id":982949,"title":"","content":"OhmygodtheEntitlementsareawesomelemmeplaythemalrea dy-<br /> <br /> Ahem.<br /> <br /> I meant to say I am quite a fan of the three example noble orders, their rules, and the creativity of privileges. Also, my first Justicar character is going to name his incubus Burroughs.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Still don't see a way to avoid being knocked down to Clarity 0 if hit with an aggressive power, though. I can see the logic, but still, there should be a sidebar-like in the Huntsmen section, since they're all about eroding it-that the ST needs to have at least permission to erode changelings to unplayable nutcases. And have at least a couple ways to restore sanity to one the player doesn't really want to abandon a perfectly good character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-06-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:31:27-07:00","id":982962,"title":"","content":"Aw, I had been hoping Incite Bedlam was going to have its Wyrd requirement lowered.<br /> <br /> Also slightly disappointed that Clarity is still added to Clash of Wills dice pools with Kenning instead of replacing it or adding the Perception bonus. We've been playtesting with that and it's WAY too high; I've yet to fail a Clash of Wills because of it (I managed to get to Clarity 10, but even when I was at 7).<br /> <br /> That said, I'm very very happy with the new Dream Rules. Very happy. Both for crossover compatibility and because I simply like them better now from a standalone mechanical standpoint too. I like that the differing dice pools were cut down a little without entirely being as empathy-dependent as in 1e, too.<br /> <br /> Also very much like the new merits in general. Well, newly revealed.<br /> <br /> I still wish Oaths could be sworn with non-changelings.<br /> <br /> I think that covers my initial thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:03:44-07:00","id":983013,"title":"","content":"It refers to pledges granting glamour, but it says nothing about that in the pledge section.<br /> <br /> Love the entitlements.<br /> <br /> The Oddments/Goblin Fruit rules make sense. I'm glad generic goblin fruit are explained.<br /> <br /> Great new merits.<br /> <br /> The Vice vs. Mien/Mask thing is confusing.<br /> <br /> The new dreamwalking rules are cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:33:38-07:00","id":983027,"title":"","content":"I'll note: I'm not going to answer every question here. Depends on the time I've got. I WILL say though, this isn't the final, final. I'm just working on a deadline, so I can't do everything I might otherwise. I will definitely be doing some tinkering in the errata pass, and perhaps before the errata pass depending on things like editing and White Wolf approvals timelines. So some of the &quot;sad this didn't change&quot; comments will definitely be addressed. Particularly if they occur in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:47:02-07:00","id":983035,"title":"","content":"The Touchstone and Exotic Airs merit are missing from the merit sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:49:13-07:00","id":983037,"title":"","content":"I can't find where it lists by wyrd how many Pledges a Changeling can hold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:52:21-07:00","id":983040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983037#post983037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't find where it lists by wyrd how many Pledges a Changeling can hold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Follow that train to the station it stops at, because there's not an error here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T19:01:01-07:00","id":983069,"title":"","content":"The Court Contract Hoard is listed as using Wyrd in its dice pool, but should use Mantle instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T19:41:19-07:00","id":983088,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit disappointed the mechanical crossover between dropping the mask and embracing the wyrd hasn't been taken care of.<br /> <br /> Seems a bit silly that dropping your mask gives you a contract bonus EXCEPT when you do it in conjunction with embracing the wyrd. Like, can you drop the mask for not-free (spend the Glamour) and get the contract bonus as well? Or can you only drop it for free with no mechanical effect?<br /> <br /> It seems a bit ambiguous to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:03:52-07:00","id":983103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983088#post983088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit disappointed the mechanical crossover between dropping the mask and embracing the wyrd hasn't been taken care of.<br /> <br /> Seems a bit silly that dropping your mask gives you a contract bonus EXCEPT when you do it in conjunction with embracing the wyrd. Like, can you drop the mask for not-free (spend the Glamour) and get the contract bonus as well? Or can you only drop it for free with no mechanical effect?<br /> <br /> It seems a bit ambiguous to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been wondering about this as well, but I definitely think it's implied you can spend the glamour and reap the rewards.<br /> <br /> To throw my own little &quot;This didn't change?&quot; in along with everyone else's, does anyone else think Light-Shy and Night's Subtle Distractions are too alike, thematically and mechanically? Light-Shy seems simply better than the other, for the same dot level of Contract. I'm not sure what could be changed, but I think they could use more distinction.<br /> <br /> To be more positive, I've got a lot of love for Entitlements in this edition, and the Principality of the Crooked Tongue is bullying me personally by being a perfect fit for my character but requiring Wyrd 4 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:41:07-07:00","id":983120,"title":"","content":"I do like the hedgefruit section, most of them seem mechanically useful. Seems pretty simple to make your own as well as they seem to have about the strength of a particularly strong condition or whatnot, so you could basically just get a bunch of interesting conditions and make them hedgefruit effects. I did always like goblin fruit though, so this is good.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Pledges, it looks like Sealings are your simple &quot;good neighbours pledge for the session&quot; and Oaths are the nuclear option, but there's not anything of a sort of a middle ground for like &quot;allies against a common foe for a season&quot; type pledges. I suppose you could use a strengthened Seal, but that just doesn't quite have the same oomph, I guess, especially as you can just dismiss a seal if you've got Wyrd it seems. Although it doesn't seem there's any actual system to it, if willed a Sealing is just dismissed automatically?<br /> <br /> I suppose the other question is - can you pledge a Keeper in some way? There doesn't seem to be any obvious alternative to the 1E &quot;make a supernaturally binding bargain with a Fae&quot; represented mechanically. (Yes, I quite liked the 1E Legate of the Black Apple a lot)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983103#post983103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering about this as well, but I definitely think it's implied you can spend the glamour and reap the rewards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd just rather it be explicit simply because I know it's the first question I'm going to get asked at the table when I run a game when someone would choose to embrace the wyrd. I'd happily houserule it either way, but I'd prefer not to if I didn't need to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 10-06-2016, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:27:53-07:00","id":983137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983120#post983120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of Pledges, it looks like Sealings are your simple &quot;good neighbours pledge for the session&quot; and Oaths are the nuclear option, but there's not anything of a sort of a middle ground for like &quot;allies against a common foe for a season&quot; type pledges.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an Oath to me. Just make sure to specify in the terms of the Oath that the alliance is temporary. Then, after the agreed upon time passes, the participants can end the alliance without the Wyrd defining them as Oathbreakers. Though, I would rule they don't continue to recieve the benefits of the Oath once the duration has ended, as the nature of the relationship the Oath defines changes at that point, to something like &quot;former allies who vanquished a mighty foe together,&quot; or &quot;former allies who failed to defeat their mutual enemy.&quot; No Oathbreaker Condition because you didn't violate the terms, no benefit because you're no longer bound to be allies.<br /> <br /> I don't know if that's the intent or not, but it seems like a reasonable interpretation to me. Might be worth adding a sentence or two to touch on if there is still the opportunity to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983120#post983120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose you could use a strengthened Seal, but that just doesn't quite have the same oomph, I guess, especially as you can just dismiss a seal if you've got Wyrd it seems. Although it doesn't seem there's any actual system to it, if willed a Sealing is just dismissed automatically?</div> </div> </div> </div>To cancel a Sealing someone is attempting to place on you, you just spend a point of Glamour and it's &quot;countered&quot;, so to speak. If you have Wyrd and you don't cancel it, you gain a Beat for allowing your word to be sealed. That's your only opportunity to cancel it, you can't allow the Sealing and then change your mind later (although the character who placed the seal can dismiss it at any time for free, so I guess you could try to convince them to release you from the Pledge.) If anything, I feel like that would give Sealings <i>more</i> weight among Changelings, since the Sealed party could have easily cancelled the Sealing, but willingly allowed themselves to be bound to their word by the Wyrd. The consequences may be fairly minor, but it's still a meaningful gesture that they allowed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:31:05-07:00","id":983139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983120#post983120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you can just dismiss a seal if you've got Wyrd it seems. Although it doesn't seem there's any actual system to it, if willed a Sealing is just dismissed automatically?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have Seal-happy Milton to thank for this being something we addressed directly in the course of running Water Under the Bridge:<br /> <br /> You can't undo a Sealing any later than as it's being made. That's why you get a Beat for letting it happen; because now you're <i>stuck with it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:55:10-07:00","id":983191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983137#post983137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like an Oath to me. Just make sure to specify in the terms of the Oath that the alliance is temporary. Then, after the agreed upon time passes, the participants can end the alliance without the Wyrd defining them as Oathbreakers. Though, I would rule they don't continue to recieve the benefits of the Oath once the duration has ended, as the nature of the relationship the Oath defines changes at that point, to something like &quot;former allies who vanquished a mighty foe together,&quot; or &quot;former allies who failed to defeat their mutual enemy.&quot; No Oathbreaker Condition because you didn't violate the terms, no benefit because you're no longer bound to be allies.<br /> <br /> I don't know if that's the intent or not, but it seems like a reasonable interpretation to me. Might be worth adding a sentence or two to touch on if there is still the opportunity to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that seems quite reasonable outside of the stated text stating that Oaths are for life. Storied relationships built out of those more transient Oaths sounds pretty good and I think I'll run with that even if there's no support for it in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983139#post983139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have Seal-happy Milton to thank for this being something we addressed directly in the course of running Water Under the Bridge:<br /> <br /> You can't undo a Sealing any later than as it's being made. That's why you get a Beat for letting it happen; because now you're <i>stuck with it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so the Glamour requirement for dismissing a Sealing was removed because someone was wasting everyone's Glamour with frivolous Sealings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T00:17:12-07:00","id":983197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983191#post983191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so the Glamour requirement for dismissing a Sealing was removed because someone was wasting everyone's Glamour with frivolous Sealings?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we had to check that the intent was that settled Sealings stick because Vector's character agreed to being Sealed by NPCs twice in as many days for Beats and the question of whether the consequent obligations could be shaken off without greater consequence than some lost points of Glamor then resulted in that information being within the realm of our direct experience.<br /> <br /> Milton himself has yet to Seal anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T00:26:31-07:00","id":983199,"title":"","content":"Aha, gotcha!<br /> <br /> That makes more sense than what I was thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T03:44:13-07:00","id":983238,"title":"","content":"I haven't given the file a good look, but I am liking the updates made to the Entitlements. Now, I can get to work doing a conversion for some of my favorite 1E groups like the Pilgrims of the Endless Road. xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T04:34:11-07:00","id":983249,"title":"","content":"Yeah the rules for creating entitlements make updating or creating entitlments easy, its excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T05:22:50-07:00","id":983257,"title":"","content":"I didnt understand the primal fundation thing, i need be elemental seeming to have it? I need a merit ? A contract? Ir i just mecanic considera my body is the own element i play by that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:35:48-07:00","id":983279,"title":"","content":"It's the first edition name for the elemental seeming effect of the Phantom Glory contract. So you either need to be an elemental or have purchased the power as an upgrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:38:14-07:00","id":983281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983279#post983279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the first edition name for the elemental seeming effect of the Phantom Glory contract. So you either need to be an elemental or have purchased the power as an upgrade.</div> </div> </div> </div>so o just need expand one point of exp on cloak of elements to get that primal fundation thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:39:21-07:00","id":983282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983191#post983191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that seems quite reasonable outside of the stated text stating that Oaths are for life. Storied relationships built out of those more transient Oaths sounds pretty good and I think I'll run with that even if there's no support for it in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Oath I described is for life. Like I said, after the agreed-upon amount of time passes, the relationship is still being defined by the Oath, it just stops being &quot;allies united in a common cause&quot; and starts being &quot;former allies who's cause is no longer pressing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:54:18-07:00","id":983289,"title":"","content":"Really enjoying reading this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983040#post983040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Follow that train to the station it stops at, because there's not an error here.</div> </div> </div> </div>There definitely is an error here, since it says that Wyrd determines how many pledges, and then never says how many. So either it's an error that is says pledges are limited by wyrd score or an error that it doesn't say how many pledges you can get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983281#post983281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so o just need expand one point of exp on cloak of elements to get that primal fundation thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, point of xp on phantom glory. Which means having to buy phantom glory to get even the 1 dot elemental battling merit which seems... unusual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-07-2016, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:27:29-07:00","id":983299,"title":"","content":"You only need Cloak of Elements for the first four. Phantom Glory (elemental) is needed for the fifth and <i>only</i> the fifth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:30:24-07:00","id":983303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983289#post983289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really enjoying reading this.<br /> <br /> <br /> There definitely is an error here, since it says that Wyrd determines how many pledges, and then never says how many. So either it's an error that is says pledges are limited by wyrd score or an error that it doesn't say how many pledges you can get.<br /> <br /> <br /> No, point of xp on phantom glory. Which means having to buy phantom glory to get even the 1 dot elemental battling merit which seems... unusual.</div> </div> </div> </div> No you only need Phantom Glory and the Elemental affinity for it for for the 5th dot of Elemental Battle, its kind of odd way for a prerequiste to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:31:15-07:00","id":983305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983299#post983299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You only need Cloak of Elements for the first four. Phantom Glory (elemental) is needed for the fifth and <i>only</i> the fifth.</div> </div> </div> </div> I got ninja'd <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:34:00-07:00","id":983367,"title":"","content":"I can't seem to find it... is the first dot of Mantle free still?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:21:45-07:00","id":983561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983367#post983367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't seem to find it... is the first dot of Mantle free still?</div> </div> </div> </div>You get it for free as part of the oath. Though the character creation rules should probably say that.<br /> <br /> Also, I can't tell if the extra skill speciality thing is meant to be for all changelings or just some changelings kiths (my computers too buggy right now to actually read through the kiths chapter so I can't check) since it's not the character creation section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:27:06-07:00","id":983722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983561#post983561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get it for free as part of the oath. Though the character creation rules should probably say that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character creation rules work out mathematically to an implication that the first dot of Mantle now costs one of your ten starting Merit dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:49:53-07:00","id":983735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983722#post983722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character creation rules work out mathematically to an implication that the first dot of Mantle now costs one of your ten starting Merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>The creation rules should probably actually say that then since I don't think most groups are going to math it out, and are more likely to go off the fact that the game says you get the dot for free as part of joining rather than it costing anything.<br /> <br /> I mean, even if it does cost starting merits, that means that it's better mechanically if you start the game with character just &quot;before&quot; they join a court so that they basically get 11 merit dots. Now I don't expect many storytellers to let players do that, but it's abit odd from a game design point of view.<br /> <br /> In my opinion they should probably put a sentence in the &quot;Choose a court&quot; step that says if you want to be part of a Court you Have to spend one of your starting merits on it, just to make sure it's clear for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-07-2016, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T21:01:14-07:00","id":983741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983735#post983735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the fact that <b>the game says you get the dot for free</b> as part of joining</div> </div> </div> </div>I search in vain for this statement.<br /> <br /> The game says you get the first dot in Mantle by swearing a societal oath to join a Court, which frankly strikes me as more of a prerequisite than a waiver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T21:06:20-07:00","id":983743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983741#post983741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I search in vain for this statement.<br /> <br /> The game says you get the first dot in Mantle by swearing a societal oath to join a Court, which frankly strikes me as more of a prerequisite than a waiver.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it says you gain a dot of the mantle merit when you take the oath and gives mechanics for how you take the oath. Also, none of the oaths require you to get the benefit and then spend external things to get the benefit that it already says it's given you, that's the point of the oaths having benefits.... that they give the benefits that they say they give. The mechanics say if you do x, then y happens. So if you do x, then y happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-08-2016, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T07:00:20-07:00","id":983901,"title":"","content":"I've been busy reading The Devil You Know, the excellent Grand Finale of the Brimstone Angels Saga, to comment much here, but I've finished it so here are my thoughts.<br /> <br /> Dreamform and Dreamwalking rules are awesome, I had been concerned when I heard the rules were being rewritten to fit the already existing dream form rules, that what made the original dreamwalking rules cool would be gone, but not only were they maintained, they were improved.<br /> <br /> They now work fine with Mages, Goetics, and Beasts, while maintaining cool ideas like the too solid tilt, but also add some cool stuff.<br /> <br /> Changelings are paradoxically more powerful, but also more vulnerible in dreams. They've been juiced up, but at the cost of it being possible to actually kill them in dreams even without the Too Solid Tilt.<br /> <br /> A Changeling with Wyrd 10, 2 Resolve, 2 Stamina will have Physical Health 17 and Dream Health of 22, +10 to speed, ect...<br /> <br /> Very powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-08-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:09:02-07:00","id":983940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=983743#post983743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it says you gain a dot of the mantle merit when you take the oath and gives mechanics for how you take the oath. Also, none of the oaths require you to get the benefit and then spend external things to get the benefit that it already says it's given you, that's the point of the oaths having benefits.... that they give the benefits that they say they give. The mechanics say if you do x, then y happens. So if you do x, then y happens.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree, it seems clear that swearing the Oath to your Court grants one mantle dot.<br /> <br /> Hypothetical I could see an Oath to another court being designed to grant a dot in Court Goodwill, hypothetically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T06:31:04-07:00","id":984368,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if Wyrd adds to physical Health in a dream, but I do agree that they're significantly more powerful there than they were before.<br /> <br /> Two things come to mind- firstly, can other supernatural beings like Mages or Beasts use Oneiromachy? And secondly, I distinctly remember in an earlier version of the Dream rules that if Intensity exceeded a certain point the character woke up immediately and remembered the dream in vivid detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:14:40-07:00","id":984411,"title":"","content":"First off, thank you for letting us look at the evolution of the gameline and being so open. I look forward to buying the final product on release! Overall, this is a fantastic job with a lot of good ideas. Hats off to the writers / devs. Going to do a look for errors and points of confusion pass.<br /> <br /> Character Creation<br /> * A &quot;create Motley&quot; step or sidebar may be prudent here, since Oaths can affect your beginning traits and are things some (but not all) groups will want to think about at the start.<br /> * An aside, a &quot;Climbing the Ladder&quot; (VtR2e) style process for creating courts would be a neat thing to introduce in a later session or web thing. Or maybe a fan could do it as a post on a forum.<br /> * Should mention that the first dot of Mantle is free here if that's the case, otherwise you get someone who only has read character creation and doesn't add it. Or an &quot;oops&quot; moment when they realize it and have to go back to adjust points. The example character creation implies it isn't free, in which case the section under Oaths confuses me.<br /> * Character Creation mentions Virtue and Vice, but later on the document says Masque and Mien.<br /> * Putting Size under &quot;Derived Traits&quot; implies, RAW, that Changelings in dreams increase their size by their Wyrd. I'm not sure this is an actual problem, since size is somewhat meaningless in dreams.<br /> * Experience Costs are listed twice, but that's probably deliberate. They also don't match, and the first one mentions &quot;Morality.&quot;<br /> * I like how the theme/mood of the game is reinforced through the examples you provide. It definitely feels like Changeling, even here.<br /> <br /> Changeling Rules<br /> * An aside, a merit to let a Changeling strengthen the mask for longer periods of time would be cool for those Changelings who try to live as humans. 1 Glamour / day or something.<br /> * Strangely, Iron can be affected by Contracts (i.e. &quot;Control Elements [Metal]&quot;). Maybe it shouldn't be? I see literally every table that plays Changeling that I've been at rule it that way.<br /> * Embracing the Wyld being mutually exclusive with dropping the Mask is interesting. Probably a balance decision. Does dropping the mask with embracing the wyld also call the Huntsman?<br /> * You decided to not make Bedlam something that happens at a lower Wyrd?<br /> * This section says that Wyrd limits the number of Pledges a Changeling may have access to, but no limit is actually given either here or in the Pledges section.<br /> * No Seeming Blessing requires the expenditure of Glamour, despite the section on Glamour saying they frequently do.<br /> * The Exotic Aires merit is mentioned but not listed. I assume it's deliberate.<br /> * With Clarity, I feel the lack of listed penalties means Changelings rarely lose clarity from breaking points. I've played two Changelings, both with a Wits + Composure of 6, and have never failed a breaking point roll. One hits breaking points frequently, since he's a therapist that has &quot;use magic to alter someone's mind&quot; as a breaking point.<br /> * Using Willpower to add Clarity to resist or contest supernatural powers is <i>extremely </i>powerful.<br /> * &quot;instead add her Clarity to her dice pool in a Clash of Wills (see p. XX).&quot; is a bit vague. Does it replace the attribute, the wyrd, or both? Also, with how high Clarity gets, this may slant the dicepool too much in a Changeling's favor. Unless it replaces both, in which case it's fine.<br /> * The Touchstone merit is mentioned, but we don't get to see it. Assuming this is deliberate as well.<br /> <br /> Dreamwalking<br /> * Love the new rules. Much more easily compatible with other gamelines.<br /> * I like how the number of different rolls were cut down. It looks like Changelings need Persuasion, Occult, Empathy, Expression to be &quot;an oneiromancer.&quot;<br /> * Dream Riding doesn't mention making small edits to a dream now. Is that covered under Dreamscaping?<br /> * I like Dreamscaping being much easier now.<br /> * My therapist character wishes Psychotherapy was better at curing conditions, since many don't require a roll to cure them. Maybe as a merit?<br /> * &quot;After creating the same dream three times in three nights and spending a point of glamour with each to imprint it upon the dreamer, the victim's mind is sent into an unnatural, obsessive spiral.&quot; The way this is placed in the text is weird. I think the intent is an explanation for how reoccurring dreams are made, but the way it is in the text implies that it can be done with any dream?<br /> * With Hedgespinning, and Tokens in general, it's not clear whether or not someone crafting tokens / hedgespun stuff pays for it if they make it after creation.<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> * Does Acute Senses apply even when Clarity drops below 7? Also, VtR2e has a merit by the same name... I'm not sure if they matters or not? Probably not.<br /> * Bounty has been a merit me and my table have wanted for a long time. Thank you.<br /> * Defensive Dreamscaping should probably add &quot;while within a dream&quot; to the last line.<br /> * Can a Changeling take Diviner? It's prerequisite is Lucid Dreamer, implicitly the merit, which Changeligns can not take. Also, taking it above one dot feels like a meh investment, but that's just me.<br /> * Elemental Battle mentions Become the Primal Foundation, which isn't a thing anywhere else in the document.<br /> * Elemental Battle's first dot mentions that it increases the damage dealt to people who attack the Changeling with Brawl or Weaponry attacks. Cloak of the Elements no longer does that by default. Is this dot meant to add that functionality?<br /> * Aside: I swear you would save so much wordcount if you made rounding up Wyrd in calculations that use half the user's Wyrd a default rule.<br /> * Any chance of getting Hungry Leaping Flames to use a more brain-y dicepool? :P<br /> * On that note. As written Hungry Leaping Flames can be used without the Contract active. Is that intended?<br /> * Hungry Leaping Flames doesn't subtract defense. Is that intended?<br /> * Fae Mount is still hard capped at 5 dots! How can we have epic steeds?<br /> * Hedgespun offers an uncapped bonus to Defense, which may be an issue. The &quot;Catch&quot; should probably be part of the Drawback since it's not a token. Also, what happens if I don't spend a dot to make it equipment or a raiment?<br /> * Should Hedgespun have a system for offering better weapons/armor?<br /> * Does Legendary Language allow the Changeling to speak some sort of Omni-Language or does it give the Changeling Language [Everything that fits the criteria] as separate languages?<br /> * Prophet is strangely written. It seems to be an intrinsic quality of the Changeling, but it mentions using mortal's dreams. &quot;A character can only benefit... once per story&quot; implies that other people could somehow get the condition, even though I don't think that's the case? I feel like most of the rules text could be replaced with &quot;Once per Story, your character may choose to have a Prophetic Dream. This could be her own dreams, or represent visiting a mortal she shares a pledge with.&quot;<br /> <br /> Goblin Fruit<br /> * Yay Goblin Fruit! Been waiting for this one.<br /> * Scarthistle is interesting. Do the tattoos count against your limit once they are tattoos? Do multiple tattoos stack?<br /> * Mantaesthetic Tea and Thistleflower need durations.<br /> * Over all, I like these. I'm left wanting more, but I can wait for the book.<br /> <br /> Pledges<br /> * Good clarification that only Changelings can negate Sealings (and Huntsmen with a roll).<br /> * It's mentioned elsewhere that Pledges can gain Glamour, but there is no mechanic for that.<br /> * Are Pledges no longer how one Ensorcells mortals?<br /> <br /> Tokens<br /> * Gossamer Raiment refers to itself as a merit. Is this accurate?<br /> * There seems to be an unusual amount of overlap between Gossamer Raiment and Hedgespun Raiment. Is this a duplication?<br /> <br /> Entitlements<br /> * Yay entitlement rules! Another thing I was looking forward to, and I'm glad it didn't disappoint.<br /> * On Entitlement Privledges, I think the Token option is meant to be that it costs a number of points equal to twice the token's value?<br /> * Can Privledge Tokens by stolen or used by someone else? Presumably they can't be created outside the entitlement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 10-09-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T09:13:29-07:00","id":984456,"title":"","content":"Contracts<br /> * Cloak of the Elements could be clearer about the immunity not applying to attacks (assuming that's the case?).<br /> * Changeling Hours is absolutely, positively bannanas. It seems to work at a range, and it's resisted by size. Freeze someone's shoes in time! Basically guarenteed to succeed and it effectively immobilizes them, potentially permanently. The effects on people and flora are also hard to parse. This contract needs serious looking at, please.<br /> * Under Light-Shy, &quot;The target&quot; under the darkling bonus is a bit weird. The contract doesn't have a target. Also does the wizened bonus also grant the ability to be perfectly motionless? I feel like it should.<br /> * Does Vainglory activate up to all three effects at once, or only one at a time?<br /> * Same question with Thorns and Brambles.<br /> * With Control Elements, how powerful are the tilts that are created? How does attacking with the element actually work? Are we talking magneto style control metal or &quot;roll around the ground as best you can&quot; style control metal? <br /> * While the AoE version of Pipes of the Beastcaller is awesome, is there a chance for a version that just affects one animal? Like the ability to call a cat or a specific cat without also calling every cat in a two to three mile radius?<br /> * Should Hidden Reality have a resist or contested roll for the Fairest benefit? Then again its effects are largely narrative and minor.<br /> * You mentioned Hedgewall actually summoning the Hedge into the mortal world and being shapable, etc. Is that going to be a thing? It sounded really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T09:27:34-07:00","id":984458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=984456#post984456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contracts<br /> * Changeling Hours is absolutely, positively bannanas. It seems to work at a range, and it's resisted by size. Freeze someone's shoes in time! Basically guarenteed to succeed and it effectively immobilizes them, potentially permanently. The effects on people and flora are also hard to parse. This contract needs serious looking at, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume clothing counts as part of the person wearing it, at least for the time stop effect. Just seems to make more story-logic sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T09:29:23-07:00","id":984460,"title":"","content":"At best that just means you need the fairest bonus. At worst it just means you need to be more clever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T10:31:40-07:00","id":984484,"title":"","content":"&quot;* Embracing the Wyld being mutually exclusive with dropping the Mask is interesting. Probably a balance decision. Does dropping the mask with embracing the wyld also call the Huntsman?&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a difference between Dropping the Mask action, and simply removing the mask as part of Embrace the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> For removing the mask as part of Embrace the Wyrd its free, because they're are no mechanical effects if you choose to do so, it just to make your self more showy while weildjng Embracing the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Dropping the Mask on the other hand its a potent magical act that requires you spend on Glamour directly on it, which empowers its effects, so you get the mechanical effects, good and bad.<br /> <br /> So they're very different actions, but not mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> So for example you can Drop The Mask in turn 1, then Embrace the Wyrd in round 2 and enjoy the benifits and draw backs of both at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T10:33:44-07:00","id":984488,"title":"","content":"I think Legendary Language is intended to be like Mage High Speech, but you can lie with it, and it provides no bonuses, it just lets you communicate with any speaking human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T12:56:45-07:00","id":984561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=984484#post984484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;* Embracing the Wyld being mutually exclusive with dropping the Mask is interesting. Probably a balance decision. Does dropping the mask with embracing the wyld also call the Huntsman?&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a difference between Dropping the Mask action, and simply removing the mask as part of Embrace the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> For removing the mask as part of Embrace the Wyrd its free, because they're are no mechanical effects if you choose to do so, it just to make your self more showy while weildjng Embracing the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Dropping the Mask on the other hand its a potent magical act that requires you spend on Glamour directly on it, which empowers its effects, so you get the mechanical effects, good and bad.<br /> <br /> So they're very different actions, but not mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> So for example you can Drop The Mask in turn 1, then Embrace the Wyrd in round 2 and enjoy the benifits and draw backs of both at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, this doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> The benefits of dropping the mask don't come about because you drop it, they come about because you don't have a mask up. There's no reason that it wouldn't take effect in <i>any</i> situation where you lack a mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:04:13-07:00","id":984637,"title":"","content":"So I think Dropping the Mask is actually about more then just exposing your mein, which is what Vainglory and choosing to reveal you mien when Embracing the Wyrd really is,your not dropping your mask at all.<br /> <br /> Okay think of you mask a white t-shirt. Dropping the Mask is taking your shirt off, Embracing the Wyrd and Vainglory gives you the option of soaking your shirt till its 100% transparent, showing everyone what's underneath, but technically even fully exposed, your shirt is still on. Your shirt being the Mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T18:37:17-07:00","id":984698,"title":"","content":"That's a nice metaphor, and maybe the one that the rules implies. However, the flavor text does not. If you drop your mask for free, you are dropping your mask for free. Except there's no benefit (are there downsides re: calling huntsmen, etc?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T18:46:58-07:00","id":984702,"title":"","content":"OH! A thing. With Entitlements granting an approach. Extra approaches are actually weaknesses against the Huntsmen because it splits your focus and it gives them extra sources of yearning--*unless* the approach has a specified order like the personal approach does. Is it intended for Entitlements to be a boon against fae but a weakness to huntsmen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T18:54:34-07:00","id":984706,"title":"","content":"what page are the entitlements on in the pdf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T20:02:20-07:00","id":984725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=984702#post984702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is it intended for Entitlements to be a boon against fae but a weakness to huntsmen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Joining an entitlement is specifically listed as one of the sources of Personal Approaches. They work the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T20:58:35-07:00","id":984738,"title":"","content":"So with the updates to how kiths work and with me looking at the potent kith merit you could destroy some peoples days as a witchtooth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T21:04:26-07:00","id":984740,"title":"","content":"I'm not really sure how Approaches could be conceived of as a weakness. Yes, they give Yearning to Huntsmen that follow them, but that's meant as an incentive for the Huntsmen to follow the Approach to begin with, and to take advantage of that Yearning they need to follow the Approach that forces them into a predictable course of action.<br /> <br /> If you're in a Court (with high Mantle) you gain a Personal Approach, if you join an Entitlement you gain a Personal Approach. I'm sure there's other ways to gain one, but I can't recall them off the top of my head right now. It's a pretty solid way to help guide a Huntsman's behaviour, and a way to force a True Fae into a course of action that plays to your strengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T21:09:03-07:00","id":984741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=984740#post984740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're in a Court (with high Mantle) you gain a Personal Approach, if you join an Entitlement you gain a Personal Approach. I'm sure there's other ways to gain one, but I can't recall them off the top of my head right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking a formal role in your Court or freehold is another one.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/930212-ctl-water-under-the-bridge-2e-playtest-ap?p=952981#post952981\">The Surveyor of Chicago</a>, for instance, gets a Personal Approach despite that being a position with no Mantle prerequisite held by maybe four separate people in the last century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T21:10:13-07:00","id":984742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=984740#post984740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure how Approaches could be conceived of as a weakness. Yes, they give Yearning to Huntsmen that follow them, but that's meant as an incentive for the Huntsmen to follow the Approach to begin with, and to take advantage of that Yearning they need to follow the Approach that forces them into a predictable course of action.<br /> <br /> If you're in a Court (with high Mantle) you gain a Personal Approach, if you join an Entitlement you gain a Personal Approach. I'm sure there's other ways to gain one, but I can't recall them off the top of my head right now. It's a pretty solid way to help guide a Huntsman's behaviour, and a way to force a True Fae into a course of action that plays to your strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly what I see.<br /> <br /> You force one of the most cunning and/or powerful adversaries in the world to play by your rulebook, and you've read it longer than they have. You know what to look for when you suspect Arcadia's coming back, and if you see them before they see you seeing them, you've got the first move advantage, and a way to starve the Huntsmen of Yearning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T05:17:43-07:00","id":984829,"title":"","content":"Every approach is a seperate strategic point you need to defend against huntsmen and another source of yearning. It gets better! Its a strategic point that offers you no benefit.<br /> <br /> Approaches, vs. Huntsmen are basically ways to set traps and defenses. &quot;They will definately do A&quot; is useful in that regard. &quot;They might do A, but they may also do B, C or D&quot; is less useful.<br /> <br /> Of course, against the True Fae every approach is an added layer of defense, so it may be worth it anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T07:33:10-07:00","id":984868,"title":"","content":"Huntsmen don't <i>have</i> to use an approach. If you only have one, they'll know it will make them predictable and not use it. <br /> <br /> So it's non a question of predictable vs multiple choice, it's a question of multiple choice vs random.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T07:50:04-07:00","id":984875,"title":"","content":"I thought the way approaches work is that to get the point of yearning, a huntsmen has to met them all. So its not more vulnerible points as one that gets narrower and narrower as there are more prerequistes for each personal approach you add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:12:14-07:00","id":984886,"title":"","content":"They need to abide by a personal approach before they can use a court approach, but it's unclear whether or not this grants any yearning by itself. (as in, two different bits of previewed stuff definitively say either way)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:05:57-07:00","id":985170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=984740#post984740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure how Approaches could be conceived of as a weakness. Yes, they give Yearning to Huntsmen that follow them, but that's meant as an incentive for the Huntsmen to follow the Approach to begin with, and to take advantage of that Yearning they need to follow the Approach that forces them into a predictable course of action.<br /> <br /> If you're in a Court (with high Mantle) you gain a Personal Approach, if you join an Entitlement you gain a Personal Approach. I'm sure there's other ways to gain one, but I can't recall them off the top of my head right now. It's a pretty solid way to help guide a Huntsman's behaviour, and a way to force a True Fae into a course of action that plays to your strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Someone who doesn't think Approaches are a massive advantage has not watched enough Burn Notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T06:17:31-07:00","id":985374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=985170#post985170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. Someone who doesn't think Approaches are a massive advantage has not watched enough Burn Notice.</div> </div> </div> </div> I love that show!!! Exactly you force the enemy to go after in a way that you have the advantage!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:01:02-07:00","id":985702,"title":"","content":"Could the extra skill speciality be added to character creation section during editing, some people I've talked to didn't realise that all changelings got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:06:58-07:00","id":985830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=985702#post985702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the extra skill speciality be added to character creation section during editing, some people I've talked to didn't realise that all changelings got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll get it added during errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:50:30-07:00","id":985867,"title":"","content":"I really love the Tempest Knights. They have that martial &quot;all for one and one for all&quot; attitude that I adore, and I think they do a better job of making it possible to balance membership with other court or motley obligates than similar 1e entitlements did. Not necessarily easy, but possible, and the elemental maelstrom imagery is a nice bonus. I think their special ability is really cool but it scales pretty alarmingly. Get five Tempests together and they're all casting like they were Wyrd 9 minimum. Especially if they invest in the elemental fighting style (which is amazing, great concept, solid mechanics) that's a recipe for a Captain Planet Curbstomp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:07:04-07:00","id":988307,"title":"","content":"Clarification needed.<br /> <br /> Gargantuan says you gain half your wyrd in size, but it doesn't say whether you should round up or down.<br /> On other kiths it states whether it should be rounded up or down. (Up, up up!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:24:46-07:00","id":988445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=988307#post988307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarification needed.<br /> <br /> Gargantuan says you gain half your wyrd in size, but it doesn't say whether you should round up or down.<br /> On other kiths it states whether it should be rounded up or down. (Up, up up!)</div> </div> </div> </div>The kith rules say &quot;If a kith blessing uses half of your Wyrd dots for an effect, always round this result up.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T21:50:04-07:00","id":988692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=988307#post988307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarification needed.<br /> <br /> Gargantuan says you gain half your wyrd in size, but it doesn't say whether you should round up or down.<br /> On other kiths it states whether it should be rounded up or down. (Up, up up!)</div> </div> </div> </div>There should be a clause at the beginning of the section/chapter that says you always round up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T07:21:39-07:00","id":988849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=988692#post988692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There should be a clause at the beginning of the section/chapter that says you always round up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, it does.<br /> <br /> Which is strange, because some Kiths say &quot;Round up&quot; while others say &quot;Round down&quot;. You'd assume it would only clarify &quot;Round down&quot; if up was the norm.<br /> <br /> Thank you, none the less!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T12:27:53-07:00","id":988978,"title":"","content":"Looking back through the Contracts, am I reading it right that Cloak of the Elements now lets you select a different element each time you activate it? I'm so used to 1e where it was fixed at purchase and you could buy other elements for 1xp, but the writing here makes no mention of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:09:36-07:00","id":989105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=988849#post988849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, it does.<br /> <br /> Which is strange, because some Kiths say &quot;Round up&quot; while others say &quot;Round down&quot;. You'd assume it would only clarify &quot;Round down&quot; if up was the norm.<br /> <br /> Thank you, none the less!</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That's just totally errata oversight stuff. I need to delete all those clauses within the Kiths themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:13:57-07:00","id":989107,"title":"","content":"Do you have any hacker type kiths? I imagine some true fae want to understand computers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:54:15-07:00","id":989197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=989107#post989107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any hacker type kiths? I imagine some true fae want to understand computers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet. Maybe down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T22:48:49-07:00","id":989224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=989107#post989107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any hacker type kiths? I imagine some true fae want to understand computers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am down with this to a point of reconsidering some things in the future. Faerie tales and cyberpunk must be married, I say!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T23:02:49-07:00","id":989228,"title":"","content":"For computer changelings I'd tweak the Author kith for programmers, use Chimera for a changeling that gets many different programs put into them, Cleareyes for surveillance software, gargantuan for a changeling that was used as datastorage, tweaked gravewright that works with angels rather than ghosts for gentry that lent the changeling out to the GM for infrastructure, levinquick for code, makers already make excellent hakers, manikin are good for living code, oracle as changeling google.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=989224#post989224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am down with this to a point of reconsidering some things in the future. Faerie tales and cyberpunk must be married, I say!</div> </div> </div> </div>I did always like those 1e token prosthetics, though their catches were harsh iirc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-18-2016, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T23:29:19-07:00","id":989235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=989228#post989228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did always like those 1e token prosthetics, though their catches were harsh iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, they were giving you a clause of a Universal Contract with a use discount for the price of a Merit in a system where that only becomes an experience point surcharge at the fourth-dot level and every core Universal Contract plus several of the supplementary ones was getting its use cost reduced to &quot;free&quot; once you activated the token for the scene, which didn't require the catch to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T23:37:32-07:00","id":989236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=989235#post989235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness, they were giving you a clause of a Universal Contract with a use discount for the price of a Merit in a system where that only becomes an experience point surcharge at the fourth-dot level and every core Universal Contract plus several of the supplementary ones was getting its use cost reduced to &quot;free&quot; once you activated the token for the scene, which didn't require the catch to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would explain why they made catches harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T04:27:23-07:00","id":989288,"title":"","content":"Now I want a True Fae who was &quot;inspired&quot; by the God machine and is super interested in the mortal world. Sends most of its changelings to the mortal world to orchestrate events such that classic stories happen (its &quot;infastructure&quot;) but gives those changelings enough rope to walk away and &quot;fall&quot; as &quot;demons.&quot; Maybe deliberately makes their koth so when they escape it becomes more demonic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:23:46-07:00","id":989319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=989224#post989224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am down with this to a point of reconsidering some things in the future. Faerie tales and cyberpunk must be married, I say!</div> </div> </div> </div>And thus the Shadowrun realm was born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:16:36-07:00","id":989336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/982644-updated-changeling-rules-chapter?p=989319#post989319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And thus the Shadowrun realm was born.</div> </div> </div> </div>Courts of Shadow already happened, I just figure it should go the other way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T23:58:12-07:00","id":990829,"title":"","content":"Hoping I'm not too late\u2026<br /> <br /> I feel that crafting Breaking Points deserve mention in the character creation section, rather than being solely buried in the Clarity section. One thing I love about ChroD character creation is that it incorporates your character's hopes and fears into the design process: hopes in the form of Aspirations, and fears in the form of Breaking Points. Crafting your character's Breaking Points goes a long way toward establishing who your character is, and deserves at least some mention in character creation, if only to say \u201ccraft your Breaking Points now; see p.XX for details.\u201d<br /> <br /> EDIT: the way I would do it would be to add a paragraph under the Clarity entry in character creation that states that you should select two Breaking Points at character creation: and then list what the two should be. Followed by a page reference to the section that goes into it in more depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-22-2016, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T00:30:34-07:00","id":990837,"title":"","content":"Wondering if Murkblur's version of the Blinded Tilt is equivalent to the one-eye intensity or the both-eyes intensity.<br /> <br /> The latter seems a bit extreme for a four-dot clause translated to a two-dot Contract, as well as being not quite in keeping with the description of what it does, and having the both-eyes version be the exceptional success effect strikes me as a more natural extension of the Contract's effect than &quot;they're deafened as well as blinded.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}